Upstream-Status: To upstream [xsimd::make_sized_batch only searches xsimd's native per-ISA architectures, never the "emulated" XSIMD_DEFAULT_ARCH fallback finufft's own xsimd.hpp wires in for architectures with no native xsimd backend at all (e.g. riscv64 built without the vector extension, our baseline here); not yet submitted upstream]

On riscv64 without -march=...v (our baseline, since the vector extension isn't
guaranteed hardware and this repo's wheels must run on any riscv64), xsimd
detects no native architecture and finufft/xsimd.hpp falls back to
XSIMD_DEFAULT_ARCH=emulated<128>. That fallback is only wired into
xsimd::default_arch - xsimd::make_sized_batch (used by min_simd_width,
GetPaddedSIMDWidth and PaddedSIMD to search for a SIMD batch of a given
width) only searches xsimd::supported_architectures, which is built purely
from native per-ISA detection and never includes "emulated". So every width
probed comes back void, min_simd_width's doubling search overflows uint8_t
(128 -> 256) with no match ever found, and every constexpr call sites
depending on it (get_padding, PaddedSIMD, ...) fail to compile - this is what
fails "Build finufft 2.5.1 py3-none-manylinux_riscv64" in CI with errors like:

  error: 'constexpr auto finufft::spreadinterp::{anonymous}::get_padding()
  [with T = double; unsigned char ns = 28]' called in a constant expression
  error: no matching function for call to 'min_simd_width<double, (128 * 2)>()'
  error: narrowing conversion of '256' from 'int' to 'unsigned char'

Bound the search by xsimd::default_arch's own batch size and fall back to
xsimd::batch<T, default_arch> directly once no native match exists, instead
of growing the probed width past it. This leaves native-architecture
platforms (x86_64, aarch64, ...) byte-for-byte unaffected, since there
default_arch resolves to the same architecture as before and the native
search always finds a match before reaching this bound - verified by
comparing finufft::utils::GetPaddedSIMDWidth<T, N>() for every N in [4, 16]
and both T=float/double, compiled natively with -mavx2, before and after this
patch (identical). Verified the patched src/spreadinterp.cpp now
cross-compiles cleanly for riscv64 (-march=rv64gc, no vector extension,
riscv64-linux-gnu-g++ 13) with zero errors, where it previously failed with
the exact error chain seen in CI; also verified under qemu-riscv64 that the
resulting padded SIMD widths are sane (2 for double, 4 for float - the fixed
128-bit emulated batch, as intended).

diff --git a/include/finufft/finufft_utils.hpp b/include/finufft/finufft_utils.hpp
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/include/finufft/finufft_utils.hpp
+++ b/include/finufft/finufft_utils.hpp
@@ -18,7 +18,14 @@ namespace finufft::utils {
 template<class T, uint8_t N = 1> constexpr uint8_t min_simd_width() {
   // finds the smallest simd width that can handle N elements
   // simd size is batch size the SIMD width in xsimd terminology
-  if constexpr (std::is_void_v<xsimd::make_sized_batch_t<T, N>>) {
+  // on platforms with no native xsimd architecture (e.g. riscv64 without the
+  // vector extension), xsimd::make_sized_batch never matches any width since
+  // it only searches native architectures, not xsimd::default_arch's
+  // "emulated" fallback - bound the doubling by that fallback's own width
+  // instead of overflowing uint8_t looking for a width that will never match
+  if constexpr (N >= xsimd::batch<T, xsimd::default_arch>::size) {
+    return xsimd::batch<T, xsimd::default_arch>::size;
+  } else if constexpr (std::is_void_v<xsimd::make_sized_batch_t<T, N>>) {
     return min_simd_width<T, N * 2>();
   } else {
     return N;
@@ -47,7 +54,15 @@ template<class T, uint8_t N> constexpr std::size_t GetPaddedSIMDWidth() {
   // helper function to get the SIMD width with padding for the given number of elements
   // that minimizes the number of iterations

-  return xsimd::make_sized_batch<T, find_optimal_simd_width<T, N>()>::type::size;
+  constexpr std::size_t width = find_optimal_simd_width<T, N>();
+  // same fallback as min_simd_width: no native xsimd architecture matches
+  // "width" exactly (e.g. riscv64 without the vector extension), so use the
+  // fixed-width "emulated" default_arch batch directly instead
+  if constexpr (std::is_void_v<xsimd::make_sized_batch_t<T, width>>) {
+    return xsimd::batch<T, xsimd::default_arch>::size;
+  } else {
+    return xsimd::make_sized_batch<T, width>::type::size;
+  }
 }
